# ChromaPilot Cursor Rules & Initialization

When asked to initialize, set up, or run this repository:

1. Run `./setup.sh --install` (or `./setup.sh`) to compile the release binary and validate prerequisites.
2. The MCP server binary is at `mcp-server/target/release/chromapilot`.
3. Cursor configuration is pre-configured in `.cursor/mcp.json`:
   ```json
   {
     "mcpServers": {
       "chromapilot": {
         "command": "${workspaceFolder}/mcp-server/target/release/chromapilot",
         "args": ["--port", "9222"]
       }
     }
   }
   ```
4. Instruct the user to load the unpacked extension from `<repo-root>/extension` at `chrome://extensions/`.
5. When automating browser tasks, always prioritize `execute_browser_pipeline` to batch multi-step actions into a single turn.
